A||||7||Pretender||need help on headder install, tips anyone?||||5||
Z||000000||Pretender||03-15-2000||05:28 PM||||I got my headders today in the mail and boy are they pretty! I went with the ones from focoa. With the pipes  came a can of vht(high temp coating) and assorted bolts and clamps. I have a few questions, <P>1. are the studs in the manifolds now(on my car) double sided? they look kinda funny.<P>2. The instructions call for removing the two rear cradle bolts to raise and lower the cradle, is this the best/easiest way? can i install with out doing this step?<P>3. A tube of copper gasket sealer is also provided, again is it better to use this or go to NAPA and get a set of new gaskets?<P>I hope you guys can anwser these few questions and provide a few hints and tips before i start this project on friday(i think). I have to spray them down a few times to coat them because i couldn't afford the extra $190 for the cer. coating. THANKS, in advance shawn.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Earne||03-15-2000||06:44 PM||||Wish I had your answers.  I do know from years of working on from the top down, any extra room for knuckles whild working on a Fiero will be appreciated.  Dropping the cradle a little sounds like a good idea and it was mentioned on another recent thread here.  I wonder if you would mind telling us what you paid for the headers including shipping?  Plus $190 if you want them jet coated?  Keep us informed on the installation, I am very interested since I talked with Phil@FOCOA about the headers after I installed the Borla exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Greg Piet||03-15-2000||07:14 PM||||I have replaced about 5 sets of stock manifolds on the v6's.  I have never had to drop the cradle.  I did have to remove, and move over the AC bracket though to get at the passenger side lowest bolt(firewall side).<BR>I also remove some bolts from the top and others from under the car(whichever is the most convenient.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pretender||03-15-2000||11:03 PM||||I paid $550 for the headders and it was $45 for the shipping and handling. A total of $595. For the "bullet-proof extra high temp racing black coating" it was an extra $190, there is another coating avail. for $140 which is the "nickle shiny surface".  I thought $45 was alittle high for shipping and my thoughts were confirmed. When i recieved the package(an old box of some sorts) with the post office stamp only costing $32. i guess all the crumpled up newspaper cost an extra $13. BUt i'm not complaining, there clearly the best headders avail. for our cars and well worth the money from what i heard. The hard part is going to be the install. I dread the thought.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Pretender||03-16-2000||12:14 AM||||Does anyone have a pic of the "2 rear engine cradle bolts"?..||||reg||5
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||03-16-2000||12:22 AM||||The 2 rear cradle bolts are easy to find. They may be hidden behind the splash shields. Look near the exhaust at the rear of the car... can't miss them. The 2 front ones go from side to side and the 2 rear bolts go up and down. If you take the 2 rear ones out then the cralde can swing down from the back(don't forget to disconnect the dogbone first)||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||03-16-2000||12:59 AM||||Pretender... Be sure to post pics and tell us what kind of performance gain!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pretender||03-16-2000||01:39 PM||||Approx. how far will the cradle lower after i loosen the 2 rear bolts and the dogbone? is there a way to "go to far" and bend something or screw something up? ||||reg||1
